package frontend

templ API() {
	<div style="max-width: 700px;margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
		<p>
			This page describes the public HTTP API of War Thunder Heatmaps. The API is free.
			To get access feel free to contact me to get your key. Provide it in
			<code>Authorization</code> request header.
		</p>
		<h3>GET /api/v1/region</h3>
		<p>
			Returns kill and death counts for each vehicle in a box of one map.
			The box is given as fractions of the tank map, from 0 to 1.
			<code>u</code> is the horizontal axis and <code>v</code> is the vertical axis.
			The two corners must differ on both axes.
		</p>
		<p>
			Query parameters:
			<ul>
				<li><code>level</code> (needed) map file name, for example <code>levels/avg_abandoned_town.bin</code>. The map selector on the main page uses the same values.</li>
				<li><code>u0</code>, <code>v0</code>, <code>u1</code>, <code>v1</code> (needed) the two corners of the box</li>
				<li><code>killTimeMin</code>, <code>killTimeMax</code> time of the kill in the battle, in seconds</li>
				<li><code>killerBattleRatingMin</code>, <code>killerBattleRatingMax</code> battle rating range of the killer vehicle, integers just how snail does it, inspect frontend selector to see how it is</li>
				<li><code>victimBattleRatingMin</code>, <code>victimBattleRatingMax</code> the same for the victim vehicle</li>
			</ul>
		</p>
		<p>
			The answer is a JSON array. Each element has these fields:
			<ul>
				<li><code>vehicle</code> internal vehicle name</li>
				<li><code>kills</code> number of kills made by that vehicle in the box</li>
				<li><code>deaths</code> number of deaths of that vehicle in the box</li>
			</ul>
		</p>
		<p>
			Status codes:
			<ul>
				<li><code>200</code> the answer is in the body</li>
				<li><code>204</code> the map is not known</li>
				<li><code>400</code> a needed parameter is missing or malformed</li>
				<li><code>500</code> something broke, let me know about it</li>
			</ul>
		</p>
		<p>
			Example:
			<br/>
			<code>curl 'https://thunder.nanachi.party/api/v1/region?level=levels/avg_abandoned_town.bin&amp;u0=0.1&amp;v0=0.1&amp;u1=0.4&amp;v1=0.4'</code>
		</p>
		<p>
			The data covers ground to ground kills in realistic battles only.
			If you want another view of the data, or images, read the
			<a href="/about">About</a> page and contact me.
		</p>
	</div>
}
